# 5. Shared Architecture and Guardrails

- Reuse the existing Custom Tables infrastructure where appropriate; avoid a separate, duplicated persistence system.
- Do not force Recruitment's monthly model onto VA Roster, Agenda, or Client Performance.
- Keep tenant-scoped definitions and data.
- Preserve the existing Member OKR, Builder, Runtime performance-history, and navigation architecture except for the specifically agreed Runtime operational-tab changes.
- Organization Admins can enable or hide provisioned tables but do not create table definitions or configure columns; CascadEffects platform/IT personnel provision definitions and columns.
- Runtime tab visibility is not the same as row visibility.
- Hiding a VA is not deleting or deactivating the VA.
- Production authorization/RLS must be verified separately; successful UI behavior or applied permission records do not prove that RLS is complete.

